WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.957
Now it is time to combine the ideas in short exercises.

00:00:03.957 --> 00:00:08.797
Start by creating variables for a fictional patient and printing them.

00:00:08.797 --> 00:00:14.822
Then inspect types for an identifier, an amount, and a Boolean flag.

00:00:14.822 --> 00:00:19.815
After that, calculate something simple such as area and perimeter.

00:00:20.485 --> 00:00:27.817
Move next to a revenue statement with formatted money, and then calculate profit and margin from sales and costs.

00:00:27.817 --> 00:00:30.302
Do not rush through the tasks.

00:00:30.302 --> 00:00:37.500
For each one, explain what the variables represent, why their types make sense, and what the output means.
